module cortado_app
kind library

# `cortado_app` is the composition root: the one place that names cortado and
# barista together and wires them onto each other.
#
# It is a sibling module rather than a package under `cortado/` for a reason
# the language enforces: a package under a module may not import its own module
# root. `cortado.component` therefore cannot name anything that assembles an
# application, which is why it asks for a `ServiceSource` — an interface over
# `std.reflect` alone — instead of knowing what a container is.
#
# A separate module has no such restriction, so the assembling that every
# `main.b` would otherwise hand-write lives here.
#
# Nothing under cortado's module root imports this, so cortado's core stays
# free of barista: an application that wants no container at all pays nothing
# for one, and cortado's own gate needs no dependency to run.
require path ".."
require github.com/beans-lang/barista v0.1.1
